WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience cheering)

2
00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.450
One of the hardest parts of "adulting",

3
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.387
I love this new term, "adulting".

4
00:00:05.387 --> 00:00:07.980
Is choosing the perfect place to live

5
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.210
and settle down and call a home. I think,

6
00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.930
I was talking about, there are chapters in life

7
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:16.010
and one of mine is the decision

8
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.210
to move from Los Angeles to New York,

9
00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.140
which was very unsettling. But,

10
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.420
I knew that it was the right thing to do.

11
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.950
It was what my daughters needed

12
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.310
and, it just, they're my north star,

13
00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.690
so I made the bold move, I took the leap.

14
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.160
I've ended up finding tremendous happiness,

15
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.740
and there are just times in our lives

16
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.710
where something happens that was unexpected,

17
00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:38.760
and we've just got to take that leap.

18
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.950
And our next guest took her own leap of faith,

19
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.410
packed up all of her belongings

20
00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.250
and moved from Chicago, Illinois

21
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.142
to the big apple, all by herself.

22
00:00:48.142 --> 00:00:49.880
(energetic music plays)

23
00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.050
Hi, I'm Moyo, and I just fulfilled my dream

24
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.380
of moving to New York city. After finishing

25
00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.320
my master's degree, I moved back

26
00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.900
into my parents' home in Chicago.

27
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.670
And even though I was so happy,

28
00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.220
I knew I needed to get out and live my life.

29
00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:06.630
So I decided to come to New York.

30
00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:10.340
I was very set on fall 2020, that was the goal,

31
00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.620
but we all know what happened, (laughs)

32
00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:17.293
the pandemic, but, I'm here now. 2021. (laughs)

33
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.350
Since I don't have a lot of space,

34
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:23.250
all of the shoes, handbags, and clothing

35
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.954
that I'm going to be buying, don't tell my dad (laughs)

36
00:01:25.954 --> 00:01:27.680
I'm going to have to find ways

37
00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.750
to be organized in my, my room.

38
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.640
So here's my room. And it was just

39
00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.160
the bed and dresser when I came in.

40
00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:40.270
So excited to fill it up and make it very homey.

41
00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.680
I just love that it's an open, like, canvas

42
00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:44.480
similar to my experience in New York,

43
00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.417
it's an open opportunity, right?

44
00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:49.090
The city of opportunities, so I'm super excited

45
00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:51.725
to decorate it and make it my home.

46
00:01:51.725 --> 00:01:53.420
(audience cheering)

47
00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.553
Please welcome, Moyo Areolu.

48
00:01:59.529 --> 00:02:02.590
Moyo Areolu. I have been thinking about you a lot.

49
00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:04.070
It is really nice to meet you in person.

50
00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.363
Nice to meet you. (laughs)

51
00:02:05.363 --> 00:02:08.220
Why did you want to come to New York?

52
00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.300
I just always wanted to live in New York.

53
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.309
Like it's, it's kinda crazy. (laughs)

54
00:02:13.309 --> 00:02:16.070
It's like an addiction. I just, I love the city.

55
00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.040
It's like a city of opportunities.

56
00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.020
The diversity, the people, the fashion, the food.

57
00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:22.853
I just love it. (laughs)

58
00:02:22.853 --> 00:02:25.530
You are so beautiful inside and out.

59
00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:29.160
And I know you think that you're just here

60
00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.810
so that we could recommend some New York places

61
00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.310
that you need to hit, but I couldn't help myself.

62
00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:39.160
I got all up involved in your design and your place,

63
00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.660
and I hope you don't mind if we now

64
00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.020
surprise you by throwing into

65
00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.248
a segment called Designed by Drew.

66
00:02:45.248 --> 00:02:48.248
(audience cheering)

67
00:02:49.713 --> 00:02:52.330
So, that is your space.

68
00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.163
Yes.

69
00:02:53.163 --> 00:02:55.270
I did want to put a brand new room

70
00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:59.190
together for you. It's behind these doors.

71
00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:01.997
So God, here we go. Open those doors.

72
00:03:01.997 --> 00:03:04.997
(audience cheering)

73
00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:07.083
I like it.

74
00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:17.240
Can I come in?

75
00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.360
Come in! This is your room.

76
00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.733
I like it! Can I sit on it?

77
00:03:21.733 --> 00:03:22.660
Now, Everything in here-

78
00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:23.690
if you like it!

79
00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:25.250
No, I like it! I love it.

80
00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:27.140
Is coming to your house and will be installed.

81
00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.494
Thank you!

82
00:03:28.494 --> 00:03:29.327
(Audience cheering)

83
00:03:29.327 --> 00:03:33.061
I like it! (laughs)

84
00:03:33.061 --> 00:03:33.894
I like it a lot.

85
00:03:33.894 --> 00:03:34.727
Really?

86
00:03:34.727 --> 00:03:36.180
I do. I really love the color,

87
00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.900
But I love the clean look (laughs)

88
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.486
Nerve-racking designing it-

89
00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.000
No, I like it!

90
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.550
Before you really get to know someone,

91
00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:48.220
but I did find out some of your likes and dislikes.

92
00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.040
Now I'll take you through a couple of reasons

93
00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.194
of why I chose certain things.

94
00:03:53.194 --> 00:03:58.194
First of all, I loved the pops of color,

95
00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.618
with like, you know, pop art.

96
00:04:01.618 --> 00:04:02.598
Yes!

97
00:04:02.598 --> 00:04:04.959
I just, I wanted colored pillows,

98
00:04:04.959 --> 00:04:06.360
but if you are not feeling as bold that day,

99
00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.780
you just remove the pillows and you have

100
00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:13.530
a gorgeous white bed that is alluring and calming.

101
00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:16.001
And, by the way, when you have these spaces,

102
00:04:16.001 --> 00:04:20.120
move stuff around, you know, edit, change,

103
00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.880
like, all of the sudden, this completely

104
00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.900
went from a lot of color to a lot less color.

105
00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:26.733
Yeah.

106
00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:30.200
I chose this because there is a real discrepancy

107
00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.120
out there in the marketplace of basically

108
00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.780
couches that can go at the foot of your bed,

109
00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:39.410
nobody wants to sit on a bench.

110
00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:41.020
You don't, I'm sorry. You know what?

111
00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:44.190
It becomes your outdoor closet.

112
00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.023
That's true.

113
00:04:45.023 --> 00:04:48.370
But, if you can actually be able to sit comfortably,

114
00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:50.950
then your room can become a social hub

115
00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.530
and you're not sitting on your bed.

116
00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:53.363
It's true.

117
00:04:53.363 --> 00:04:55.010
But, most couches are honestly

118
00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.890
way too high to be at the foot of your bed.

119
00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:00.670
And this is a problem. So, my suggestion is

120
00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:03.560
you actually trim the legs and lower them.

121
00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.430
But the couch at the end of the bed

122
00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.050
opens it up to being able to hang out in there.

123
00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:08.883
Right.

124
00:05:10.589 --> 00:05:12.580
And then, when it comes to lamps,

125
00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:16.500
my Cardinal rule is don't go with a metal shade

126
00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.290
or an opaque shade. You will not get light from those.

127
00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:22.250
You'll get up and down light, but you,

128
00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.580
I am obsessed with shades that actually

129
00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.610
let the whole light glow.

130
00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:27.443
Yeah.

131
00:05:27.443 --> 00:05:28.820
And don't get me started on can lighting,

132
00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.450
whoever invented can lighting,

133
00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:32.134
I'd like to meet you in a dark alley

134
00:05:32.134 --> 00:05:33.789
(laughs)

135
00:05:33.789 --> 00:05:38.720
by the way, no woman looks good in can lighting.

136
00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.227
Do you ever go in the bathroom and you're like

137
00:05:40.227 --> 00:05:44.720
"oh my God, where did all my self-confidence go?"

138
00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:45.785
Can lighting!

139
00:05:45.785 --> 00:05:47.050
(audience laughs)

140
00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.610
Because overhead lighting makes you look

141
00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.339
like you're starring in your own personal mugshot.

142
00:05:52.339 --> 00:05:53.172
(audience laughing)

143
00:05:53.172 --> 00:05:55.180
So, I also love this headboard

144
00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.360
and chose it because I thought

145
00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.330
it was unique in the marketplace,

146
00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.650
because it goes behind the nightstands.

147
00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:01.483
Ah!

148
00:06:01.483 --> 00:06:02.670
And if you notice, most headboards

149
00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.399
would be cut off right here.

150
00:06:04.399 --> 00:06:07.843
Okay! Well, here you go. It's all coming with you!

151
00:06:08.995 --> 00:06:09.966
Thank you!

152
00:06:09.966 --> 00:06:10.799
(audience cheering)

153
00:06:10.799 --> 00:06:12.390
And, thank you.

154
00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:13.223
Thank you, thank you.

155
00:06:13.223 --> 00:06:15.801
I really appreciate your time.

156
00:06:15.801 --> 00:06:19.134
(uplifting music plays)

